refactor(get): unify JSON envelope to {matches, results: []}

The --json output of 'get' had two shapes depending on input syntax:

  get <xpath>     -> data: <node>            (single-result object)
  get selected    -> data: {matches, results: [...]}
  query <type>    -> data: {matches, results: [...]}

Consumers had to dispatch on the path syntax before parsing — a single
jq pipeline could not absorb both. Aliasing single-path 'get' onto the
already-existing 'results: []' envelope removes the
